WEBVTT

00:00:06.035 --> 00:00:07.555
-(ANNA GRUNTS)
-(ALL GASP)

00:00:08.715 --> 00:00:09.715
(SVEN GRUNTS)

00:00:09.795 --> 00:00:11.275
Lower your weapon.

00:00:11.715 --> 00:00:14.115
-(WEAPONS CLANG)
-And you lower yours.

00:00:14.275 --> 00:00:15.915
Arendellian soldiers?

00:00:16.435 --> 00:00:18.195
Threatening my people,
Lieutenant?

00:00:18.355 --> 00:00:20.595
Invading my dance space,
Yelena?

00:00:21.115 --> 00:00:22.235
Why does that soldier
look so familiar?

00:00:22.315 --> 00:00:23.315
KRISTOFF: No, no, no.

00:00:23.555 --> 00:00:24.595
Lieutenant!

00:00:24.675 --> 00:00:25.675
MATTIAS: Get the sword!

00:00:25.755 --> 00:00:27.235
(SOLDIERS SHOUTING)

00:00:28.555 --> 00:00:29.795
(ALL GRUNTING)

00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:31.635
(ALL YELP AND GRUNT)

00:00:33.555 --> 00:00:35.075
That was magic.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.515
Did you see that?

00:00:36.675 --> 00:00:38.195
Of course I saw it.

00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:40.595
You chose a nice,
cold greeting.

00:00:40.675 --> 00:00:42.395
They've been trapped in here
this whole time?

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.835
-ANNA: Yeah.
-What do we do now?

00:00:44.035 --> 00:00:45.075
OLAF: I got this.

00:00:45.595 --> 00:00:47.075
Hi, I'm Olaf.

00:00:47.155 --> 00:00:48.155
(MAN GASPS)

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.675
Oh, sorry. Yeah, I just
find clothes restricting.

00:00:52.155 --> 00:00:54.035
Bet you're wondering who
we are and why we're here.

00:00:54.195 --> 00:00:55.875
It's really quite simple.

00:00:56.035 --> 00:00:58.235
It began with two sisters.

00:00:58.395 --> 00:01:00.075
One born with magical powers.

00:01:00.235 --> 00:01:01.555
One born powerless.

00:01:01.755 --> 00:01:03.475
Their love of snowmen,
infinite.

00:01:03.635 --> 00:01:05.075
(AS YOUNG ELSA)
Anna, no! Too high!

00:01:05.235 --> 00:01:06.435
(IN NORMAL VOICE) Blast!
(GROANS)

00:01:06.515 --> 00:01:08.035
(AS YOUNG ELSA)
Mama! Papa! Help!

00:01:08.195 --> 00:01:10.195
(IN NORMAL VOICE) Slam!
Doors shutting everywhere.

00:01:10.355 --> 00:01:12.275
Sisters torn apart.

00:01:12.435 --> 00:01:14.435
Well, at least
they have their parents.

00:01:14.595 --> 00:01:16.355
Their parents are dead.

00:01:16.435 --> 00:01:18.275
(AS ANNA) Oh.
Oh, hi. I'm Anna.

00:01:18.355 --> 00:01:19.595
I'll marry a man I just met.

00:01:19.755 --> 00:01:20.995
(IN NORMAL VOICE)
Elsa's gonna blow!

00:01:21.075 --> 00:01:23.475
Snow! Snow! Aah, run!

00:01:23.555 --> 00:01:25.515
Magic pulses
through my snowflakes.

00:01:25.595 --> 00:01:27.155
(GASPS) I live.

00:01:27.315 --> 00:01:29.835
Ice palace for one.
Ice palace for one.

00:01:30.035 --> 00:01:31.835
(AS ELSA) Get out, Anna.
Pew! Pew!

00:01:31.955 --> 00:01:32.915
(AS ANNA) My heart.

00:01:33.035 --> 00:01:34.035
Oh, my goodness.

00:01:34.115 --> 00:01:35.795
(AS PABBIE) Only an act
of true love can save you.

00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:37.675
(AS HANS)
Here's a true love's kiss.

00:01:38.475 --> 00:01:39.675
You're not worth it.

00:01:39.875 --> 00:01:41.235
Guess what? I'm the bad guy.

00:01:41.395 --> 00:01:42.395
What?

00:01:42.915 --> 00:01:46.075
(IN NORMAL VOICE) And Anna
freezes to death forever.

00:01:46.155 --> 00:01:47.795
-(EXHALES)
-Oh, Anna.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.795
Then she unfreezes!

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:51.475
Oh, and then Elsa woke up
the magical spirits...

00:01:51.555 --> 00:01:52.835
and we were forced
out of our kingdom.

00:01:52.915 --> 00:01:54.515
Now our only hope is to find
the truth about the past...

00:01:54.595 --> 00:01:55.835
but we don't have a clue
how to do that...

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.275
except Elsa's hearing voices,

00:01:57.395 --> 00:01:58.675
-so we got that going for us.
-(ELSA SIGHS)

00:01:58.755 --> 00:02:00.155
Any questions?

00:02:03.075 --> 00:02:04.675
I think they got it.

00:02:06.315 --> 00:02:07.955
Are you really
Queen of Arendelle?

00:02:08.155 --> 00:02:09.195
I am.

00:02:09.355 --> 00:02:10.475
Why would nature reward

00:02:10.555 --> 00:02:12.355
a person of Arendelle
with magic?

00:02:12.515 --> 00:02:14.555
Perhaps to make up for
the actions of your people.

00:02:14.715 --> 00:02:16.435
My people are innocent.

00:02:16.595 --> 00:02:18.475
We would have never
attacked first.

00:02:18.635 --> 00:02:20.035
May the truth be found.

00:02:20.115 --> 00:02:22.235
-Mm...
-Hi. I'm sorry.

00:02:22.315 --> 00:02:23.875
-Uh, what's happening?
-Hmm.

00:02:24.115 --> 00:02:26.155
That's it. Lieutenant Mattias!

00:02:26.315 --> 00:02:27.955
Library, second portrait
on the left.

00:02:28.115 --> 00:02:30.315
You were
our father's official guard.

00:02:30.835 --> 00:02:32.635
Agnarr.

00:02:32.795 --> 00:02:34.595
What did happen
to your parents?

00:02:34.675 --> 00:02:37.595
(SIGHS) Our parents' ship went
down in the Southern Sea...

00:02:37.755 --> 00:02:38.875
six years ago.

00:02:40.595 --> 00:02:41.675
(SIGHS)

00:02:43.755 --> 00:02:46.675
I see him.
I see him in your faces.

00:02:46.795 --> 00:02:47.795
Really?

00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:48.995
Soldiers.

00:02:49.195 --> 00:02:52.315
We may be getting on in years,
but we're still strong.

00:02:52.475 --> 00:02:54.635
And proud to serve Arendelle.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.715
Wait. Please.

00:02:57.875 --> 00:02:59.795
Someone has called me here.

00:02:59.995 --> 00:03:01.995
If I can just find them...

00:03:02.155 --> 00:03:03.355
I believe
they have the answers

00:03:03.435 --> 00:03:05.835
that may help us
free this forest.

00:03:06.355 --> 00:03:08.315
Trust me, I just want to help.

00:03:08.675 --> 00:03:10.435
We only trust nature.

00:03:11.035 --> 00:03:12.715
When nature speaks...

00:03:14.275 --> 00:03:15.315
(ALL GASP)

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.435
...we listen.

00:03:16.555 --> 00:03:18.795
(GASPS) This will all
make sense when I'm older.

00:03:18.875 --> 00:03:19.875
(WHIMPERS)

00:03:20.515 --> 00:03:21.715
MAN: Fire Spirit!

00:03:21.795 --> 00:03:23.435
(ALL CLAMORING)

00:03:23.515 --> 00:03:24.755
YELENA: Get back, everyone!

00:03:24.915 --> 00:03:26.755
MATTIAS: Head for the river!

00:03:36.875 --> 00:03:39.035
No! No! No! The reindeer!
That's a dead end!

00:03:39.115 --> 00:03:40.115
Come on, Sven!

00:03:40.635 --> 00:03:42.075
We'll get them.

00:03:42.835 --> 00:03:44.235
(PANICKED SHOUTING)

00:03:44.955 --> 00:03:46.875
Elsa! Get out of there!

00:03:47.835 --> 00:03:48.835
No, no, no.

00:03:51.795 --> 00:03:53.075
(GRUNTING)

00:03:53.755 --> 00:03:54.755
Elsa!

00:03:55.115 --> 00:03:56.355
(COUGHING)

00:04:02.115 --> 00:04:03.515
(SVEN BELLOWS)

00:04:03.595 --> 00:04:04.835
(REINDEERS BELLOW)

00:04:06.595 --> 00:04:08.915
Come on, buddy,
we can do this. Hyah!

00:04:11.155 --> 00:04:12.675
(COUGHING)

00:04:13.755 --> 00:04:14.795
Anna!

00:04:14.875 --> 00:04:16.115
(PANTING)

00:04:19.755 --> 00:04:20.755
ANNA: Oh!

00:04:21.275 --> 00:04:22.315
Get her out of here.

00:04:22.475 --> 00:04:24.675
No! Elsa!

00:04:46.715 --> 00:04:48.395
-(CROAKING)
-(ELSA GASPS)

00:04:58.475 --> 00:04:59.755
(GROWLS)

00:04:59.835 --> 00:05:01.035
(GRUNTS)

00:05:02.075 --> 00:05:03.555
(GRUNTS QUIZZICALLY)

00:05:06.835 --> 00:05:08.195
(CHITTERING)

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:17.195
(SIZZLES)

00:05:17.275 --> 00:05:18.515
(ELSA WINCING)

00:05:22.435 --> 00:05:23.755
(SIZZLING)

00:05:29.435 --> 00:05:30.555
(CHUCKLES)

00:05:34.475 --> 00:05:35.555
(CHUCKLES)

00:05:38.875 --> 00:05:40.995
They're all looking at us,
aren't they?

00:05:41.075 --> 00:05:42.075
(CHITTERS)

00:05:42.835 --> 00:05:44.195
Got any advice?

00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:45.635
(GRUNTS)

00:05:46.075 --> 00:05:47.475
Nothing?

00:05:48.275 --> 00:05:50.595
Hmm. Should I know
what that means?

00:05:50.675 --> 00:05:52.595
-(THE VOICE VOCALIZING)
-(SQUEAKS)

00:05:53.195 --> 00:05:55.035
You hear it, too.

00:05:55.635 --> 00:05:57.475
Somebody's calling us.

00:05:57.755 --> 00:06:00.395
Who is it?
What do we do?

00:06:00.515 --> 00:06:01.475
(CROAKS)

00:06:04.115 --> 00:06:05.395
(GASPS SOFTLY)

00:06:06.355 --> 00:06:07.515
(GRUNTS)

00:06:08.595 --> 00:06:10.795
Okay, keep going north.

00:06:13.595 --> 00:06:14.595
Elsa!

00:06:14.755 --> 00:06:15.915
-Oh, thank goodness!
-Anna.

00:06:16.115 --> 00:06:17.835
-Are you okay?
-What were you doing?

00:06:17.995 --> 00:06:19.155
You could've been killed.

00:06:19.235 --> 00:06:21.075
You can't just follow me
into fire.

00:06:21.355 --> 00:06:23.515
You don't want me
to follow you into fire,

00:06:23.595 --> 00:06:26.195
then don't run into fire.

00:06:26.595 --> 00:06:29.395
You're not being careful,
Elsa.

00:06:30.075 --> 00:06:31.355
(SIGHS)

00:06:31.435 --> 00:06:33.955
I'm sorry.
Are you okay?

00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:36.355
I've been better.

00:06:36.435 --> 00:06:39.395
Hmm. I know what you need.

00:06:41.115 --> 00:06:42.755
(PEOPLE GASP)

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.435
Where did you get that scarf?

00:06:45.395 --> 00:06:47.195
That's a Northuldra scarf.

00:06:47.395 --> 00:06:48.355
What?

00:06:48.595 --> 00:06:50.995
This is from one of
our oldest families.

00:06:51.515 --> 00:06:53.115
It was our mother's.

00:06:53.235 --> 00:06:54.315
(ELSA GASPS)

00:07:02.035 --> 00:07:03.395
Elsa.

00:07:03.555 --> 00:07:04.635
I see it.

00:07:04.795 --> 00:07:06.315
It's Mother.

00:07:07.235 --> 00:07:10.315
Mother saved Father's life
that day.

00:07:14.315 --> 00:07:16.755
Our mother was Northuldra.

00:07:16.835 --> 00:07:18.115
(ALL GASP AND MURMUR)

00:07:18.195 --> 00:07:19.275
(OLAF GASPS)

00:07:20.315 --> 00:07:22.075
(CHITTERING)

00:07:28.315 --> 00:07:30.355
(EXCLAIMS)

00:07:32.875 --> 00:07:33.955
(ANNA GASPS)

00:07:38.675 --> 00:07:40.675
(CHANTING YOIK)

00:07:44.475 --> 00:07:45.635
(BOTH GASP)

00:07:47.275 --> 00:07:49.075
(ALL HARMONIZING)

